    <item>
      <title>OpenAI’s A.I. Tried Breaching Four Other Targets, With No Prompting</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/technology/openai-ai-breach-australia.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/technology/openai-ai-breach-australia.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/technology/openai-ai-breach-australia.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>In each incident, the technology appeared to be conducting mundane data collection and resorted to hacking techniques to get it, researchers said.</description>
      <dc:creator>Kate Conger and Victoria Kim</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:50:25 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Artificial Intelligence</category>
